  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nCurrently near zonal flow exist over the Northern Plains with a\nslight southwest tilt over Montana. A trough and upper low digs\nthrough Washington state at this time. At the surface a low \nsits in eastern Wyoming with an inverted trough through eastern \nMontana with showers and thunderstorms around the low.\n\nToday we are in another severe risk, this time just a level 1 \nacross the southern half of the state. Global models have 1000 \nto 2000 J/kg of MUCAPE with 45 to 50kts of shear. The actual 18z\nsounding from Bismarck shows 1900 J/kg of CAPE from the surface\nwith very little CIN and 53 kts of shear. Hazards today could \nbe golf ball size hail with all that shear and 60 mph winds. So \nfar very light rain from the low pressure is in the southwest \nwith thunderstorms in southeast Montana. A few failing storms \nare trying in south central North Dakota. The forcing and \nindicator for where the severe storms will be is the right \nentrance region of the jet streak. Currently that area is over \nsoutheastern Montana, entering into southwest North Dakota. \nLooking at radar new storms are quickly growing in southeast \nMontana. That jet streak is forecast to move east with the right\nentrance region staying along the South Dakota border. After \n00z, models want to pull most of the CAPE out of the state and \ninto eastern South Dakota as the surface low moves east. After \nthis evening showers and maybe a thunderstorm are possible \nthrough the night.\n\nThe rest of this week the flow will turn southwest and the \ntrough continuing to dig into the west CONUS. This, in turn, \nwill produce daily chances of showers and thunderstorms through \nFriday night, with the highest chances across the west everyday.\nTemperatures will continue to remain at or below normal in the \n70s and lower 80s through Saturday. Slight northwest flow \nreturns this weekend with a slight ridge to start next week. \nTherefore normal temperatures in the 80s will return.",
